  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID CASA-1000 Secretariat project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Central Asia Regional):  This program assists the CASA-1000 infrastructure project, which will interlink the power systems of four contiguous countries in Central/South Asia: Kyrgyz Republic, Tajikistan, Afghanistan, and Pakistan, through support to a CASA-1000 Secretariat that provides coordination and technical assistance to all four countries. With FY 2022 funds, this activity will facilitate the transition of the CASA-1000 Secretariat functions to the CASA country delegations and other donors. The CASA-1000 project will contribute to regional economic stability and supports the South Asia Strategy that fosters linkages between Central Asia and South Asia.</narrative>
  </description>
